he \noption in this regard is exercised by the beneficiaries.  \n(d) As on 01.01.2022, 1.08 crore LPG consumers have voluntary given up their LPG \nsubsidy. State/UT-wise details are at Annexure. \n  \n\nAnnexure \nAnnexure referred to in part(d) of Lok Sabha Unstarred Question No. 296 to be answered on \n03.02.2022 regarding “5 kg Gas Cylinder Connections” by Shri Kesineni  Srinivas \nState/UT \nNumber of customers given up their LPG \nSubsidy \nAndaman and Nicobar Islands 421 \nAndhra Pradesh 2,34,009 \nArunachal Pradesh 23,638 \nAssam 1,90,400 \nBihar 4,35,425 \nChandigarh 19,204 \nChhattisgarh 1,42,696 \nDelhi 8,51,854 \nDadra and Nagar Haveli & Daman and Diu 13,968 \nGoa 46,192 \nGujarat 4,89,563 \nHimachal Pradesh 71,439 \nHaryana 3,61,652 \nJharkhand 1,02,332 \nJammu and Kashmir 1,54,762 \nKerala 3,03,645 \nKarnataka 7,54,187 \nLakshadweep 143 \nLadakh 144 \nManipur 47,121 \nMeghalaya 7,672 \nMaharashtra 17,85,126 \nMizoram 43,985 \nMadhya Pradesh 4,56,389 \nNagaland 31,670 \nOdisha 1,69,630 \nPuducherry 16,553 \nPunjab 4,14,027 \nRajasthan 7,14,552 \nSikkim 7,827 \nTelangana 3,80,492 \nTamil Nadu 6,73,958 \nTripura 18,871 \nUttar Pradesh 13,54,264 \nUttarakhand 1,56,516 \nWest Bengal 3,59,608 \nTotal 1,08,33,935 \n \nSource : OMCs. \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|8|STARRED   |297", "t": "Nuclear Radiation", "head": " \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nDEPARTMENT OF ATOMIC ENERGY \nLOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. *297 \n TO BE ANSWERED ON 23.03.2022 \n \nNUCLEAR RADIATION \n \n*297.  PROF. SOUGATA RAY: \n \nWill the PRIME MINISTER be pleased to state: \n \n(a) whether the Government has taken precautionary measures to counter the \nnuclear radiation caused by nuclear disaster , if any , due to Russia -Ukraine \nconflict; \n(b) if so, the details of such precautionary measures; \n(c) whether the Russia-Ukraine conflict will impact the safety and security of \nKudankulam Reactor in Tamil Nadu; \n(d) if so, the details thereof; \n(e) whether any demand has come up to scrap 