 374 \nANSWERED ON 3RD FEBRUARY, 2022 \n \nPROPOSAL FOR PROVISION OF SIX AIRBAGS IN CARS \n \n374.  SHRI ASADUDDIN OWAISI: \n   \nWill the Minister of ROAD TRANSPORT AND HIGHWAYS  \n \nसड़क परिवहन औि िाजमार्ग मंत्री \nbe pleased to state: \n \n(a) whether the Government proposes to make  provision of six air bags \nmandatory in all cars with  seating capacity up to eight people from \nOctober this year; \n(b)  if so, the details thereof; \n(c)  whether the Society of Indian Automobile  Manufacturers (SIAM) has \nopposed this proposal and  if so, the reaction of the Government \nthereto; and \n(d)  the rationale objective behind this move and action taken/being taken \nby the Government on the concerns raised by SIAM in this regard? \n \n \nANSWER \n \nTHE MINISTER OF ROAD TRANSPORT AND HIGHWAYS \n  \n(SHRI NITIN JAIRAM GADKARI) \n \n(a) to (d ) This Ministry, vide GSR 1483(E) dated 7th December, 2017, \nmandated the requirement of airbag for the driver, as per Automotive \nIndustry Standard(AIS) 145. The Ministry has notified GSR 148(E) dated \n2nd March, 2021 regarding mandatory provision of an airbag  for the \npassenger seated on the front seat of a vehicle, next to the driver, as per \nAIS 145, as amended from time to time for the vehicles manufactured on \nand after the 1st Day of April, 2021, in the case of new models, and 31st \nday of August, 2021, in th e case of existing models. However, due to \nCOVID 19 pandemic, this Ministry vide GSR 595(E) dated 26th August 2021 \nhas extended the timeline in respect of date of implementation of fitment \nof air bags on existing models upto 31st  December 2021. \n  \n\nThe Ministry of Road and Transport and Highways, vide GSR 16(E) \ndated 14 th January, 2022, has notified that vehicles of category M1, \nmanufactured after 01 st October 2022, shall be fitted with two side/side \ntorso air bags, one each for the persons occupying front row outboard \nseating positions and two side curtain/tube air bags, one each for the \npersons occupying outboard seating positions. This has been noti fied to \nenhance safety for the vehicle occupants. Comments and objections have \nbeen solicited from all stakeholders within a period of thirty days. \n  \n \n \n***** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|8|STARRED   |375", "t": "Renaming of Nehru Yuva Kendra", "head": " \nGovernment of India \nMinistry of Youth Affairs & Sports \n(Department of Youth Affairs) \nLOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NUMBER *375 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 29.03.2022 \nRenaming of Nehru Yuva Kendra \n*375. SHRI VISHNU DATT SHARMA: \nWill the Minister of YOUTH AFFAIRS AND SPORTS be pleased to \nstate: \n(a) whether the Government is considering  revitalization, \nreconceptualization and renaming of Nehru  Yuva Kendra so as to \nbring it in line with its  potential to contribute towards its mandate \nfor youth development; \n(b) if so, the details thereof; and \n(c) if not, the reasons therefor? \n \nANSWER \nTHE MINISTER OF YOUTH AFFAIRS AND SPORTS \n[SHRI ANURAG SINGH THAKUR] \n(a) to (c) A statement is laid on the Table of the House. \n**** \n  \n\n \nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PARTS (a) TO (c ) OF THE \nLOK SABHA STARRED QUESTION NO.*375 FOR 29.03.2022  \nREGARDING RENAMING OF NEHRU YUVA KENDRA  ASKED BY \nHON’BLE MP SHRI VISHNU DATT SHARMA: \n(a) At present, there is no such proposal under consideration. \n(b) Question does not arise. \n(c) Nehru Yuva Kendra Sangathan (NYKS) , an autonomous \norganisation under the Ministry of Youth Affairs and Sports, having \nits presence in 623 districts  with wide network of village based \nYouth Clubs with an enrolment of about 50 Lakh rural Youth has the \nmandate to generate awareness; organization and mobilize rural \nYouth between the group of 15 -29 years for developmental work in \nthe villages, with emphasis on values, vision and volunteer action.  \nYouth from all sections of the society get  opportunity to take \npart in the NYKS programs and activities. Over the years, the Youth \nhave been given opportunity to participate in adventure camps, \nNational Integration Camps, Lifeskill Education, Inter -state Youth \nExchange Programs(Ek Bharat Shreshtha Bharat) and other Youth \nexchange Programs supported by Ministry of Home Affairs, namely \nthe Tribal Youth Exchange Programs and the  North-East Youth \nExchange Programs. These programs  enable to enhance the  \nleadership qualities among the youth and also for the Youth to \nparticipate in Nation-building activities. \n**** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|8|STARRED   |376", "t": "Covid Stimulus Package for Fisheries Sector", "head": "LOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION No. 376 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 3rdFebruary, 2022 \n \nCity Gas Infrastructure \n \n376.   SHRI V.K. SREEKANDAN: \n \nपे\u0000ोिलयम और \u0000ाक ृितक गैस मं\u0000ी \nWill the Minister of PETROLEUM AND NATURAL GAS be pleased to state: \n \n(a) whether it is a fact that the Government has received as much as 430 bids for city gas \ninfrastructure in different geographical areas and if so, the details thereof;  \n \n(b) whether it is also a fact that Petroleum and Natural Gas Regulatory Board has authorized 228 \ngeographical areas in 27 States and Union territories covering approximately 53 per cent of the \ngeographical area and 70 per cent of its population and if so, the details thereof; and  \n \n(c) whether it is also true that so far 11 rounds have been held for the award of city gas \ninfrastructure and if so, the details thereof? \n \nANSWER \nपे\u0000ोिलयमऔर\u0000ाक ृितकगैसमं\u0000ालयम\u0000रा\u0000यमं\u0000ी \n(\u0000ीरामे\u0000रतेली  )  \n \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF PETROLEUM AND NATURAL GAS \n(SHRI RAMESWAR TELI) \n \n(a) to (c)Petroleum & Natural Gas Regulatory Board (PNGRB) is the authority to grant authorization to \nthe entities for developing of City Gas Distribution (CGD) network in Geographical Areas (GAs) as \nper PNGRB Act, 2006.Upto the 10th CGD bidding round, PNGRB has authorized 228 GAs, comprising \n407 districts in 27 States/UTs covering 53 per cent of the geographical area and 70 per cent of its \npopulation, for the development of CGD networks. PNGRB has launched 11 th CGD Bidding Round on \n17.09.2021 and has received 439 bids from 26 entities against 61 GAs. Letter of Intents (LoI) for 52 \nGAs have been issued by PNGRB to 13 entities. Details of GAs authorized after the 10 bidding round \n(round wise) are at Annexure \n**** \n  \n\n \nAnnexure \n \nANNEXURE REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PART (a) to (c) OF LOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 376 TO BE ANSWERED ON 03.02.2022 REGARDING \nCITY GAS INFRASTRUCTURE. \n \nDetails of GAs authorized (round wise) in the country \nS.No. Round Year  GA authorized \n1 1st Round 2008 6 \n2 2nd Round 2009 3 \n3. 3rd Round 2011 4 \n4. 4th Round 2013 9 \n5. 5th Round 2015 8 \n6. 6th Round 2015 18 \n7. 7th Round 2016 1 \n8. 8th Round 2016 6 \n9. 9th Round 2018 86 \n10. 10th Round 2018 50 \n11 Authorized by Ministry  37 \n Total  228 \n12. 11th Round 2021 Bids received for \n61 GAs \n \nSource: PNGRB \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|8|STARRED   |377", "t": "Crimes against Minor Girls and Boys", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF NEW AND RENEWABLE ENERGY \nLOK SABHA  \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 377 \nANSWERED ON 03.02.2022 \n \nPROCUREMENT AND CONSUMPTION OF GREEN ENERGY \n+377. SHRI SANJAY BHATIA \nWill the Minister of NEW AND RENEWABLE ENERGY be pleased to state: \n(a) whether the Government has proposed new rules for the procurement and consumption  \n           of Green Energy in August, 2021; \n(b) if so, the details thereof; \n(c) whether the latest rules would encourage the energy consumers including industries in       \n           Karnal Parliamentary Constituency of Haryana at large scale to avail the benefits of  \n           renewable energy sources for regular operation; and \n     (d) if so, the details thereof along with the steps taken in this regard? \n \nANSWER \n \nTHE MINISTER OF NEW & RENEWABLE ENERGY AND POWER  \n \n(SHRI R.K. SINGH) \n \n(a)to(d) Yes, the Government has proposed draft rules \"Draft Electricity (Promoting \nRenewable Energy through Green Energy Open Access) Rules, 2021\" for procurement and \nconsumption of Green Energy.  The draft rules were circulated for stakeholder consultation in \nAugust, 2021. \n \nThe proposed rules will encourage energy consumers including industries in Karnal \nParliamentary Constituency of Haryana, who are willing to consume Green power, i.e. power \ngenerated from renewable sources of energy to avail the benefits of renewable energy sources \nfor regular operation. \n \n***** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|8|STARRED   |378", "t": "Adarsh Villages", "head": "������������������� �\n������������������������������������ �\n����� ����� �\n�������������������������� �\n������������ �����������\n�\n�������������������������������������� �\n�\n���������������������������� �\n�\n�������������������������������������������������������������������\n�����������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n��������������������������������\n�������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n������������������������������������\n����������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n����������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n�\n������ �\n�\n������������������������������������������������� �\n�\n����������������� �\n�\n����� �������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n��������������������������������������������������������������������������\n������� ��������������������\n�������������������\n���� �\n������ ������\n���� � ������\n������������ �����\n���������� ������\n������������ ������\n������ �������\n�\n������������������������������������