Health Mission", "head": " \n \n \n \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF HEALTH AND FAMILY WELFARE \nDEPARTMENT OF HEALTH AND FAMILY WERLFAE  \n \nLOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO.60 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON THE 4TH FEBRUARY, 2022 \n \nINFRASTRUCTURAL DEVELOPMENT UNDER NATIONAL DIGITAL \nHEALTH MISSION \n \n*60. SHRI RAJENDRA AGRAWAL:  \n  SHRI ANIL FIROJIYA:  \n \nWill the Minister of HEALTH AND FAMILY WELFARE be pleased to state:  \n \n(a) whether the Government has assessed the requirement of infrastructure and \nadministrative support under the National Digital Health Mission;  \n \n(b) if so, the details thereof;  \n \n(c) whether the Government proposes to involve the private sector through a PPP Model \nunder various initiatives of the scheme; \n \n(d) if so, the details thereof;  \n \n(e) whether the Government has taken any steps to provide benefits of the scheme to the \npoor and those affected by digital divide; and  \n \n(f) if so, the details thereof? \n \nANSWER \nTHE MINISTER OF HEALTH AND FAMILY WELFARE  \n(DR MANSUKH MANDAVIYA) \n \n(a) to (f) A Statement is laid on the Table of the House. \n \n \n \n \n \n \n\n \n \n \n \nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO LOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. 60* FOR 4TH FEBRUARY, 2022 \n \n(a) to (f) Government of India has launched Ayushman Bharat Digital Mission \n(ABDM) which aims to create a platform enabling interoperability of health data within \nthe health ecosystem to create longitudinal Electronic Health Record (EHR) of every \ncitizen. ABDM is implemented by National Health Authority (NHA). \n \nThe infrastructure required for development of interoperable digital platform & \ncertain modules under the National Digital Health Mission (now Ayushman Bharat \nDigital Mission) has broadly been assessed and iden tified in line with the objectives of \nABDM.  \n \nFor administrative support, various policy frameworks such as Health Data \nManagement Policy, Sandbox Guidelines, Health Information Provider Guidelines etc. \nhave been prepared and issued for smooth implementation of ABDM. NHA is providing \nnecessary support including technical assistance and training, for all stakeholders to \nintegrate their solutions under ABDM ecosystem.  \n \nBoth public and private sector IT solutions in health are integrated through \nvarious regis tries under ABDM through the sandbox environment to aid creation of \nlongitudinal EHR across the country. \n \nGovernment has taken various steps to ensure that the benefits of the mission \nreach every citizen. Inclusion is one of the key principles of ABDM. The  digital health \necosystem created by ABDM supports continuity of care across primary, secondary and \ntertiary healthcare in a seamless manner. It aids availability of health care services \nparticularly in remote and rural areas through various technology int erventions like \ntelemedicine etc. \n \n***** \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|8|STARRED   |61", "t": "Establishment of Central University at Anantapur", "head": "������������������� �\n��������������������� �\n������������������������������ �\n��� ������ �\n�\n����������������������� �\n���������������������������� �\n�\n������������������ �������������������������������\n�\n����� �������������������������� �\n� ��������������������� �\n \nWill the Minister of EDUCATION be pleased to state: \n \n(a) whether the Government has approved in princip al a proposal for setting up a \nCentral  University at Anantapur, Andhra Pradesh and if so, the details thereof; \n \n(b)  the details of Government approved budget and Detailed Project Report (DPR) for \n establishment of the said Central University; \n \n(c)  whether the Government has set any target time and road map for sanctioning the \n approved budget to complete the establishment of the said University within t he \n stipulated time; and \n \n(d)  if so, the details thereof and if not, the reasons therefor? \n \n������ �\n�\n��������������������� �\n�\n������������������������� �\n \n