TATE FOR TEXTILES  \n (SMT. DARSHANA JARDOSH) \n \n(a) & (b): Under Technology Upgradation Fund Scheme (TUFS), there is no State -wise allocation \nof funds. District-wise details of subsidy released to the textile units located in the State of Tamil Nadu \nunder TUFS/Amended TUFS, since 2018-19 are given in Annexure-I. \n \n(c): With a view to streamline the procedures and to speed up the settlement of subsidy claims, the \nguidelines of ongoing Amended TUFS (ATUFS) were modified and issued on 02.08.201 8 to make \niTUFS online portal an end to end solution with features such as automatic registration of subsidy \napplications, use of digital signature, geo -tagging of assets, engraving of system generated Machine \nIdentification Codes on machinery, claim track ing facility and direct release of subsidy to beneficiary \nthrough PFMS etc. Also, various policy clarifications and delegation of financial powers to office of \nTextiles Commissioner have been issued. Further, Inter Ministerial Steering Committee in its mee ting \nheld on 22.10.2021 has approved various measures and relaxations including automated/graded \nverification of machinery to expedite settlement of claims to ensure timely disbursement of subsidies \nunder ATUFS. \n  \n\nAnnexure-I \nDistrict-wise details of subsidy released to textile units located in Tamil Nadu under \nTUFS/ATUFS since 2018-19 \nS.No. Name of District  No. of cases Subsidy amount (in \nRs. crore) \n1 Chennai 12 1.06 \n2 Coimbatore 196 26.36 \n3 Dharmapuri 1 0.13 \n4 Dindigul 25 6.80 \n5 Erode 119 24.90 \n6 Kancheepuram 1 1.52 \n7 Kanniyakumari 2 0.05 \n8 Karur 26 4.07 \n9 Madurai 16 3.99 \n10 Namakkal 84 35.33 \n11 Pudukkottai 4 0.31 \n12 Ramanathapuram 2 0.02 \n13 Salem 37 2.21 \n14 Sivaganga 2 0.90 \n15 Theni 11 4.50 \n16 Thoothukudi (Tuticorin) 4 0.06 \n17 Tiruchirappalli 8 0.10 \n18 Tirunelveli 10 0.92 \n19 Tirupur 521 62.22 \n20 Tiruvallur 4 3.36 \n21 Tiruvarur 2 0.02 \n22 Vellore 1 0.00 \n23 Virudhunagar 37 15.67 \n24 Cud