es of investors;\n \n(b)\n \nif\n \nso, the number of such cases which have cometo the notice of the \nGovernment;\n \n(c)\n \nthe amount of money mis\n-\napproriated by the said\n \nsocieties alongwith the number \nof investors who lost\n \ntheir money in the process, society\n-\nwise; and\n \n(d) \n \nthe steps taken by the\n \nGovernment in this regard\n \nto safeguard the interest of the \ninvestors?\n \n \nANSWER\n \nMINISTER OF COOPERATION\n \nसहका\u0000रता\n \nमं\u0000ी\n \n \n(SHRI\n \n \nAMIT SHAH\n)\n \n \n(a) to (d\n): A statement is laid on the Table of the House.\n \n \n \n\nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PARTS (a) TO (\nd\n) OF LOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. \n99\n \nDUE FOR REPLY ON \n8\nTH\n \nFEBRUARY, 2022\n \n \n(a) \nto\n \n(d) Yes sir. A large number of complaints have be\nen received for non\n-\nrepayment / \nmisappropriation of deposits of investors against some of the multi\n-\nstate cooperative \nsocieties in various states of the Country, including Rajasthan. In case of delinquent \nsocieties against whom complaints are received, action for winding up is taken unde\nr \nSection 86 of the Multi\n-\nState Cooperative Societies (MSCS) Act, 2002.  Presently \nwinding up proceedings is underway in case of 77 societies, a list of which is at \nAnnexure A.\n \nComplete details regarding the amount of money misappropriated by the \nsocieties\n, along with the numbers of members who lost their money is not available.\n \n\nAnnexure\n-\nA\n \nList of multi\n-\nState cooperative societies against whom liquidation proceedings \nare under way under Section 86 of the MSCS Act, 2002:\n \nSl. \nNo.\n \nName of the society\n \nState\n \n1\n.\n \n \nJatropha Growers & Bio\n-\nFuel Development Cooperative \nLtd., Hyderabad, Andhra Pradesh\n \nAndhra \nPradesh\n \n2\n.\n \n \nThe Regional Resource Development Cooperative Society \nLtd., Vijayawada, Andhra Pradesh\n \nAndhra \nPradesh\n \n3\n.\n \n \nSouth Indian Fisherman Coop. Society Ltd., \nVishakap\na