TARRED QUESTION NO. 786 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 07.02.2022 \n \nIndian Council of Social Science Research \n†786. SHRI SHANKAR LALWANI: \nWill the Minister of EDUCATION be pleased to state: \n \n(a) the annual budget of Indian Council of Social Science Research during the last \nthree years; \n \n(b) the amount of buget allocation utilised by Indian Council of Social Science \nResearch out of the total budget allocation; \n \n(c) the details of the amount given by Indian Council of Socail Science Research \nto its subordinate institutions during the last three years, Institution-wise; and \n \n(d) the details of heads under which the allocated amount has been used by \nMadhya Pradesh Council of Social Science Research during the last three years?  \n \nANSWER \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF EDUCATION \n(DR. SUBHAS SARKAR) \n \n(a) & (b): The annual budget of Indian Council of Social Science Research (ICSSR), \nNew Delhi and utilization by it during the last three years are given below: \nFinancial Year Annual Budget (Rs. in Lakh) Funds Utilized (Rs. in Lakh) \n2018-19 \n \n \n16,289.41 15,288.22 \n2019-20 14,349.96 14,129.98 \n \n \n \n \n2020-21 11,958.43 10,438.02 \n \n(c): ICSSR, New Delhi has no subor dinate institution, but has  six ( 06) Regional \nCentres. \n \n \n(d): ICSSR, New Delhi does not provide any grant-in-aid to Madhya Pradesh Council \nof Social Science Research.  \n \n***** \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|8|UNSTARRED |787", "t": "Interest Subsidy Scheme on Education Loans", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF EDUCATION \nDEPARTMENT OF HIGHER EDUCATION  \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 787 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 07TH  FEBRUARY, 2022 \n \nInterest Subsidy Scheme on Education Loans \n†787.  SHRI CHANDESHWAR PRASAD: \nWill the Minister of EDUCATION be pleased to state: \n(a)  the objective and salient features of central sector interest subsidy scheme on education \nloans; \n(b)  whether the Government has set any targets under the said schemes; and \n(c)  if so, the details thereof and the achievements made therein? \n \nANSWER \n MINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF EDUCATION \n(DR. SUBHAS SARKAR) \n \n(a) to (c): The Department of Higher Education, Ministry of Education is implementing the Central \nSector Interest Subsidy (CSIS) s cheme. The objective of the scheme is to ensure that no \nstudent is denied the opportunity to pursue higher education in professional courses because he \nor she is poor . Salient features  of the scheme is available in the web portal \nwww.education.gov.in/hi/scholarships-education-loan-4-hi. The scheme is open to all the eligible \napplicants. In 2020-21, more than 9.80 lakh claims were settled and more than Rs. 1,476 Crore \nwas disbursed under the CSIS scheme.  \n***** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|8|UNSTARRED |788", "t": "Student-Faculty Ratio at IIT", "head": " \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF EDUCATION \nDEPARTMENT OF HIGHER EDUCATION \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 788 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 07.02.2022 \n \nStudent-Faculty Ratio at IIT \n \n788.   DR. SHASHI THAROOR: \n \nWill the Minister of Education be pleased to state: \n \n(a) the details of the number of faculty members employed by Indian \n Institutes of Technology (IIT) with a breakup of reserved   categories and \n the number of vacancies at each IIT; \n \n(b) the student to faculty ratio at each IIT; \n \n(c) whether the Government has  taken any steps to address the number of \n vacancies and reach a more effective student to faculty ratio and if so, \n the details thereof and if not, the reasons therefor; \n \n(d) whether the Government is considering relaxation of reservation \n requirements in order to fill the vacancies and if so, the details thereof \n and if not, the reasons therefor; and \n(e) whether the Government has taken measures to increase the pool of \n candidates who can fulfil the qualification requirements from reserved \n categories by providing incentives of any sort and if so, the details thereof \n and if not, the reasons therefor? \n \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF EDUCATION \n \n(DR. SUBHAS SARKAR) \n \n \n(a) & (b): The details are at ANNEXURE. \n(c) to (e): IITs are autonomous insti tutes governed by the Institutes of \nTechnology Act, 1961 and the Statutes framed there under from time to time. \nFilling up of vacancies is a continuous process and IITs issue rolling \nAdvertisement, which is open throughout the year for all candidates, who fulfill \nthe required qualifications and experience for faculty positions in IITs.  \n \n\nMinistry of Education has requested all IITs to fill up the vacancies in faculty \ncadre through Special Recruitment Drive  in Mission Mode . The Ministry has \nasked IITs to fol low the reservation as per Central Education Institutes \n(Reservation in Teacher’s Cadre) Act, 2019. In Ph.D programme, candidates \nfrom reserved categories  are given relaxation in qualifying marks, application \nfees during admission process and granted fellowship so as to increase the pool \nof candidates available for the faculty posts in IITs.  \n \n***** \n\n \n \nANNEXURE \n \nANNEXURE REFERRED TO IN PART (A) AND (B) OF THE REPLY TO THE LOK \nSABHA UNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 788 TO BE ANSWERED ON 07.02.2022 \nASKED BY DR. SHASHI THAROOR, HON’BLE MEMBER OF PARLIAMENT, \nREGARDING ‘STUDENT-FACULTY RATIO AT IIT’ \n \nSl. No. Name of IIT Total \nFaculty \nin \nposition* \nFaculty \nfrom \nreserved \ncategories \n(SC/ST/OBC \n& EWS) \nTotal \nVacant \nFaculty \npost  \nStudent : \nFaculty ratio \n1 IIT Bombay 693 26 532 18:1 \n2 IIT Delhi 703 46 73 15:1 \n3 IIT Guwahati 433 39 296 17:1 \n4 IIT Kanpur 484 35 351 19:1 \n5 IIT Kharagpur 711 43 815 21:1 \n6 IIT Madras 604 82 396 19:1 \n7 IIT Roorkee 504 71 296 19:1 \n8 IIT(BHU) Varanasi 319 47 289 23:1 \n9 IIT Bhubaneswar 125 22 115 22:1 \n10 IIT Gandhinagar 115 8 45 16:1 \n11 IIT Hyderabad 258 41 132 15:1 \n12 IIT Indore 169 47 81 14:1 \n13 IIT Jodhpur 191 28 65 17:1 \n14 IIT Mandi 128 11 73 16:1 \n15 IIT Patna 122 14 100 21:1 \n16 IIT Ropar 161 28 69 16:1 \n17 IIT Tirupati 102 25 18 12:1 \n18 IIT Palakkad 96 17 24 13:1 \n19 IIT Jammu 89 18 31 12:1 \n20 IIT Bhilai 63 12 43 12:1 \n21 IIT Goa 53 12 40 13:1 \n22 IIT Dharwad 54 15 39 13:1 \n23 IIT(ISM) Dhanbad 334 92 447 21:1 \n \n*excluding adjunct and  visiting faculty "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|8|UNSTARRED |789", "t": "Conservation of Cultural Heritage and Vedic Tradition", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF CULTURE \n \nLOK SABHA \n \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 789 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 7.02.2022 \n \nCONSERVATION OF CULTURAL HERITAGE AND VEDIC TRADITION  \n789. SHRI ARUN KUMAR SAGAR: \nWill the Minister of CULTURE संˋ ृ ित मंũी be pleased to state:  \n(a) whether the Government has taken till date or  proposes to take any steps to conserve the \nculture heritage and Vedic tradition of the country  which has  taught the lesson of Guru \nBhakti, brotherhood and service of parents to the whole world; \n \n(b) if so, the details thereof; and \n \n(c) if not, the reasons therefor? \n \nMINISTER FOR CULTURE, TOURISM AND DEVELOPMENT  \nOF NORTH EASTERN REGION \n \n(SHRI G. KISHAN REDDY) \nANSWER \n(a & b)   Yes Sir.   Indira Gandhi National Centre for the Arts (IGNCA) , an autonomous body  \nunder the Ministry of Culture through its Vedic Heritage Portal  has taken steps to \ndocument and conserve the Vedic traditions of the country. The portal is in the \npublic domain  and  can be accessed at www.vedicheritage.gov.in ( it registers \nmonthly hit of approximately 6 lakhs).  This portal  is a vast resource of  textual \ndetails of Vedic Samhitas, Brahmanas, Aranayakas, Upanishad,  Vedangas, vedic \nrituals on Shrauta Sutras in audiovisual format, lists of vedic institutions and eminent \nscholars \n(c )  Does not arise. \n**** \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|8|UNSTARRED |79", "t": "Encroachment of Railway Land", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 79 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 02.02.2022 \n \nENCROACHMENT OF RAILWAY LAND \n \n79.  SHRI GNANATHIRAVIAM S.: \n \n     Will the Minister of RAILWAYS be pleased to state: \n \n(a) whether large stretches of railway land are being encroached upon \nin various parts of the country including Tamil Nadu;  \n(b) if so, the details thereof; \n(c) whether such encroachments have been causing serious \noperational and other problems;  \n(d) if so, the detai ls thereof and the reaction of the Railways thereto; \nand  \n(e) the measures taken by the Railways to remove such \nencroachments? \n \nANSWER \nMINISTER OF RAILWAYS, COMMUNICATIONS AND \n ELECTRONICS & INFORMATION TECHNOLOGY \n(SHRI ASHWINI VAISHNAW) \n \n(a) & (b): As on 31.03.2021, a total of 810.31 hectare of Railway land is \nunder encroachment in various parts of the country including  Tamil \nNadu. \n \n(c) & (d): Encroachments cause bottleneck and safety hazard in train \noperations and difficulties in track maintenance which at times affects \n\nthe line capacity and through put which ultimately affects the revenue \nof Railways. Encroachments also pose problem for execution of \ndevelopment works. \n \n(e): Railways carry out regular surveys for identifying encroachments \nand take action for their removal. If the encroachments are of \ntemporary nature (soft encroachments) in the shape of jhuggies, \njhopris and squatters, the same are got removed in consultation and \nwith the assistance of Railway Protection Force and local civil \nauthorities.  For old encroachments, where party is not amenable to \npersuasion, action is taken under Public Premises (Eviction of \nUnauthorized Occupants) Act, 1971 (PPE Act, 1971), as amended from \ntime to time.  Actual eviction of unauthorized occupants is  carried out \nwith the assistance of State Government and police. \n \n****** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|8|UNSTARRED |790", "t": "Welfare Schemes for ST", "head": " \n \n          \n \n \n \n              GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \n                 MINISTRY OF TRIBAL AFFAIRS \nLOK SABHA \n            UNSTARRED No- 790 \n             TO BE ANSWERED ON  07/02/2022 \n \n           WELFARE SCHEME FOR ST \n  \n790. SHRI KUMBAKUDI SUDHAKARAN: \n  \nWill the Minister of TRIBAL AFFAIRS be pleased to state? \n  \n(a) whether any central project monitoring units have been set up in States to oversee the implementation \nof tribal welfare schemes, as announced by the Government in November 2021; \n(b) if so, the details thereof and if not, the reasons therefor; \n(c)  the status of allocation, disbursal and utilisation of fund toward this initiative, as on date, for both \nCentral and State units; \n(d) whether the Government has set deadlines for the Central and State monitoring units to be functional; \nand \n(e)  if so, the details thereof and if not, the reason therefor? \n   \nANSWER \n  \nMINISTER OF STATE FOR TRIBAL AFFAIRS \n(SMT. RENUKA SINGH SARUTA) \n  \n(a) to (e): The Ministry of Tribal Affairs implements various Central Sector and Centrally Sponsored \nScheme through States /UT Government.  Ministry in last few years  has undergone a major strategic \nshift and has developed scheme specific portals with end to end digitization of  various processes \nensuring  physical and financial monitoring of the funds released under different schemes. \n  \nMinistry is not aware about specific announcement of the Government for setting up of PMUs in \nstates.  However, the NITI Aayog has initiated Data Governance Quality Index which evaluates various \nMinistries on data-based Governance and has advised all Ministries to set up Data and Strategy units in \nMinistry for digitization of processes related to implementation and monitoring of Central \nSector/Centrally sponsored schemes of ministries/Departments. \n  \nTill 14th Finance Cycle (from 2016-17 to 2020-21), amount ranging from 1-2% of the scheme was given \nto States/UTs as administrative cost for implementation of the Schemes. While approving the \ncontinuation of Centrally Sponsored and Central Sector Scheme for Development of STs over the 15th \nFinance Commission  (2021-22 to 2025-26), funds  have been provided to set up State Programme \nManagement Unit (SPMU) at State level  for effective implementation and monitoring of the combined \nschemes of the Ministry.  Funds  have also been earmarked under the scheme  \"Monitoring, Evaluation, \nSurvey and Social Audit\" including setting up of Central PMU.  The role of central PMU is to co- ordinate \nwith the State units for providing data in respect of various schemes.  \n***** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|8|UNSTARRED |791", "t": "Employment Generation in Tribal Areas", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF TRIBAL AFFAIRS \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO- 791 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON- 07/02/2022 \n  \nEMPLOYMENT GENERATION ON TRIBAL AREAS \n \n791.  SHRI ACHYUTANANDA SAMANTA: \n \nWill the Minister of TRIBAL AFFAIRS be pleased to state: \n  \n(a) the details of schemes that have been executed by the Government during the last five years in order \nto boost employment generation in tribal areas; \n(b)  whether employment opportunities have increased due to such schemes; \n(c) if so, the details thereof;  \n(d) the State-wise details of persons benefitted therefrom; and \n(e) the steps taken regarding tribal areas of Odisha and PVTGs in Odisha? \n \n ANSWER \n  \nMINISTER OF STATE FOR TRIBAL AFFAIRS \n(SMT. RENUKA SINGH SARUTA) \n(a) to (e) The Government has adopted a holistic approach for providing livelihood opportunities to tribal \npopulation, including tribal women through various schemes of Central Ministries as at Annexure 1.  \nNational Rural Livelihood Mission administered by Ministry of Rural Development aims at mobilizing \nall rural poor household into self help group, build institutions of poor by federating them at villages / \ncluster / Block level, provide long term support to attain appreciable increase in incomes through credit \nlinkages and multiple livelihood options. Women SHGs under DAY-NRLM consist of 10-20 persons. At \nleast one woman member from each identified rural poor household, is to be brought under the Self Help \nGroup (SHG) network. The State wise details of tribal SHGs created so far are at Annexure 2.  \nMinistry of Tribal Affairs strives to achieve inclusive and sustainable growth of tribal population in the \ncountry. The Centrally Sponsored Schemes/Grants administered by the Ministry which, inter-alia, \nsupports livelihood and employment generation for tribal population are under: \n1        Special Central Assistance to Tribal Sub-Scheme (SCA to TSS) \n2         Grant-in-aid under Article 275(1) of the Constitution \n3.        Development of Particularly Vulnerable Tribal Groups (PVTGs)  \n  \nState-wise details of beneficiaries (including Odisha) under these schemes are not centrally maintained \nin the Ministry. However, Ministry of Tribal Affairs has recently developed an online portal \n(https://grants.tribal.gov.in/adigram) to capture physical and financial progress including beneficiary \ndetails under various schemes being administered.  \n\nBesides, Ministry of Tribal Affairs, through TRIFED and NSTFDC, is implementing the following \nprogrammes/Schemes which specifically cater to livelihood / income generation needs of the tribal \npopulation: \n1. Mechanism for Marketing of Minor Forest Produce (MFP) through Minimum Support Price \n(MSP) and Development of Value Chain for MFP.  \n2.  Institutional Support for Development & Marketing of Tribal Products/Produce \n3.  Equity Support to National Scheduled Tribes Finance and Development Corporation \n(NSTFDC)/ State Tribal Finance and Development Corporations (STFDCs) \n Van Dhan Vikas Karyakram, an initiative under the Scheme ‘Mechanism for Marketing of Minor \nForest Produce (MFP) through Minimum Support Price (MSP) and Development of Value Chain for \nMFP’, targets livelihood generation for tribals by harnessing the wealth of forest i.e. Van Dhan. Under \nthis programme, it is envisaged to set-up tribal community owned Minor Forest Produce centric multi-\npurpose Kendras in predominantly tribal districts. The Kendras would act as common facility centres \nfor procurement cum value addition to locally available Minor Forest Produce. Value addition of raw \nproduce is expected to increase the value of the MFP considerably and consequently the income of the \ngatherers. \nThe National Scheduled Tribes Finance and Development Corporation (NSTFDC), under the Ministry \nof Tribal Affairs, is implementing an exclusive scheme titled “Adivasi Mahila Sashaktikaran Yojana \n(AMSY)” for economic development of Scheduled Tribes Women. Under the scheme, NSTFDC \nprovides loan upto 90% for projects costing upto ₹2.00 lakh. Financial assistance under the scheme is \nextended at highly concessional rate of interest of 4% per annum.   \nState-wise details of beneficiaries (including Odisha) under these schemes are at Annexure 3 \nMinistry of Tribal Affairs also administers an exclusive scheme namely ‘Development of PVTG’ \nspecifically for the PVTG population. A statement showing the outlay under the scheme of Development \nof PVTG in the past 5 years and released amount for each activity along with UC/PPRs pending status \nfor the State of Odisha is given below:- \nAmount (Rs. in lakh) \nFinancial Year Released by MoTA Amount Utilized by State Pending UC \n2016-17 1164.00 1164.00 0.00 \n2017-18 1297.00 1297.00 0.00 \n2018-19 3626.00 3626.00 0.00 \n2019-20 976.38 976.38 0.00 \n2020-21 1202.00 1202.00 0.00 \n2021-22 1197.00 0.00 Not yet due \n  \n  Other achievements under PVTG scheme of the Ministry in Odisha are as under:  \n  \n Ministry has engaged State Tribal Developmen"}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|8|UNSTARRED |792", "t": "Loan from JICA", "head": " \n \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF FINANCE \nDEPARTMENT OF ECONOMIC AFFAIRS \n  \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.792 \n  \nTO BE ANSWERED ON MONDAY, FEBRUARY 07, 2022 \n  \nLoan from JICA \n  \n792. SHRI HANUMAN BENIWAL: \n  \nWill the Minister of FINANCE be pleased to state: \n  \n(a) whether the Union Government proposes to make recommendation for providing loan \nfrom Japan International Cooperation Agency (JICA) for giving benefit of drinking water \nby laying pipeline parallel to the Rajiv Gandhi Lift Canal from Indira Gandhi  Canal for \n2104 villages and urban areas of Jodhpur, Barmer and Pali districts of Rajasthan;  \n(b) if so, the details thereof along with the time by which the said recommendation is likely \nto be made, and  \n(c) if not, the reasons therefor? \n  \nANSWER \n  \nMINISTER OF STATE FOR FINANCE \n(SHRI PANKAJ CHAUDHARY) \n  \n(a) to (c) :  A project proposal submitted by the Government of Rajasthan titled ‘Parallel \nCarrier System to Rajiv Gandhi Lift Canal from Indira Gandhi Main Canal (RGLC Phase -\nIII)’ seeking external assistance of Rs.1,163.20 crore from Japan International Cooperation \nAgency (JICA)   was  included in the JICA Rolling Plan on 02.07.2020, based on the \nrecommendations of Central Line Ministries and NITI Aayog.   Subsequently, the \nGovernment of Rajasthan decided to execute the project with the funds made available by the \nGovt. of India under Jal Jeevan Mission (Urban) and the State Government, and, therefore, \nrequested to drop the proposal for external funding from JICA. Accordingly, the project \nproposal has been dropped from the JICA Rolling Plan on 12.07.2021. \n**** \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|8|UNSTARRED |793", "t": "Skill Development Programme for Youth", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA  \nMINISTRY OF SKILL DEVELOPMENT AND ENTREPRENEURSHIP  \n  \nLOK SABHA  \n  \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.†793  \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 07.02.2022 \n \nSKILL DEVELOPMENT PROGRAMME FOR YOUTH \n \n†793.  SHRI DILESHWAR KAMAIT:  \nSHRIMATI GEETA KORA:  \nSHRI JYOTIRMAY SINGH MAHATO: \n \nWill the Minister of SKILL DEVELOPMENT AND ENTREPRE NEURSHIP be \npleased to state: \n \n(a) the total number of youths trained under skill development programmes in \nJharkhand, West Bengal and Bihar during the last fi ve years and the Gender-wise, Year-\nwise and the District-wise details thereof; and \n \n(b) the total number of youths have been provided j obs in Jharkhand, West Bengal \nand Bihar after getting trained under these skill d evelopment programmes Gender-wise, \nYear-wise and District-wise details thereof? \n \nANSWER \n  \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF  \nSKILL DEVELOPMENT AND ENTREPRENEURSHIP  \n(SHRI RAJEEV CHANDRASEKHAR) \n \n(a)  The Ministry of Skill Development and Entrepreneur ship (MSDE) is implementing \nits flagship demand-driven Centrally Sponsored Sche me, Pradhan Mantri Kaushal Vikas \nYojana (PMKVY), for imparting short duration skill development training through Short-\nTerm Training (STT) and Recognition of Prior Learni ng (RPL) to youth across all States/ \nUnion Territories (UTs). Details of persons trained  inJharkhand, West Bengal and \nBiharunder PMKVY year-wise, Gender-wise and Distric t-wise during last five years is at \nAnnexure-I. \n \n Jan Shikshan Sansthan (JSS) Scheme: To achieve the vision of Skilling India, \nthe JSS Competent of scheme to support voluntary ag encies for adult education and skill \ndevelopment has been transferred from Ministry of E ducation (erstwhile Ministry of \nHuman Resource Development) to Ministry of Skill De velopment and Entrepreneurship \non 2 \nnd  July, 2018. \n \nThe Jan Sikshan Sansthan (JSS) initiative is a step  in the direction of realizing the \nunique demographic potential of urban slums and rur al India. The programs are based on \nthe polyvalent or multi-dimensional approach. The m ain target of the JSS is to impart \nvocational skills to the non-literates, neo-literates and the person having rudimentary level \nof education of 8 \nth  standard i.eupto class 12 th  in the age group of 15-45 years with due \nrelaxation in case of “Divyangjan” and other deserv ing cases. Priority is given to Women, \n\nSC, ST, OBC and Minorities. Details of persons trai ned in Jharkhand, West Bengal and \nBihar under JSS year-wise, Gender-wise and District -wise during last five years is \nat Annexure II ). \n \n National Apprenticeship Promotion Scheme (NAPS):  This Scheme is for \npromoting apprenticeship training and increasing th e engagement of apprentices by \nproviding financial support to industrial establish ments undertaking apprenticeship \nprogramme under the Apprentices Act, 1961. Training  consists of Basic Training and On-\nthe-Job Training / Practical Training at workplace in the industry. Details of persons \ntrained in Jharkhand, West Bengal and Bihar under N APS year-wise, Gender-wise and \nDistrict-wise during last five years is at Annexure-III . \n \n Industrial Training Institute (ITI): MSDE provide long term training through ITIs. \nDetails of persons enrolled in Jharkhand, West Beng al and Bihar under ITIs year-wise, \nGender-wise and District-wise during last five years is at Annexure-IV .  \n \nApart from those skilled by the Ministry, the detai ls of persons trained through 3 \nmajor schemes, viz. Deen Dayal Upadhyaya Grameen Ka ushalya Yojna (DDU-GKY) and \nRural Self Employment Training Institutes (RSETI) i mplemented by Ministry of Rural \nDevelopment (MoRD) and Deen Dayal Antyodaya Yojna- National Urban Livelihood \nMission (DAY-NULM)Ministry of Housing and Urban Aff airs (MoHUA) from 2018-21 in \nWest Bengal are placed below \n \nScheme State 2018-19 2019-20 2020-21 \n (DDU-GKY) Jharkhand 9668 12866 1050 \nWest Bengal 8652 9531 521 \nBihar 10729 14301 2687 \n (RSETI) Jharkhand 17969 15911 11467 \nWest Bengal 13149 12576 5876 \nBihar 26688 24961 14868 \n (DAY-NULM) Jharkhand 11203 7107 768 \nWest Bengal 35416 4262 409 \nBihar 6400 4313 1173 \n \n \n \n(b) Total number of youth placed under PMKVY & JSS are attached at Annexure V & \nAnnexure VI  respectively. \n \nAs per the Final report on Tracer Study of ITI Grad uates (published in January \n2018 by the Ministry of Skill Development & Entrepr eneurship, GoI) shows that 63.5% of \ntotal ITI pass-outs got employed (wage+self, out of  which 6.7% are self-employed) and \n36.4% remained unemployed and was looking for jobs.   Even though the first figure was \nlow for females (55.3%) as compared to that for mal es (65.1%), the figures for SCs (65%) \nand STs (69.8%) were higher than the percentage of total pass-outs in (wage+self) \n\nemployed.But, all these figures are for the country  as a whole and not for Bihar, \nJharkhand& West Bengal only.  \n \nSince NAPS is an apprenticeship related scheme, no placement is tracked. \n \nThe details of persons placed/settled by "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|8|UNSTARRED |794", "t": "Nomination of MPs to Governing Body", "head": " \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA  \nMINISTRY OF EDUCATION \nDEPARTMENT OF HIGHER EDUCATION \n \nLOK SABHA  \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 794 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 07.02.2022 \n \nNomination of MPs to Governing Body \n \n†794. SHRI ARUN SAO: \nSHRI VIJAY BAGHEL: \nSHRI SUNIL KUMAR SONI: \n \nWill the Minister of EDUCATION be pleased to state: \n(a) the posts for which nominations are made by the Government in the governing body \nof educational institutions coming under the purview of Ministry of Education; \n \n(b) whether any eligibility criteria has been laid down by the Government for the said \nposts; \n \n(c) if so, the details thereof along with the present process of nomination; \n \n(d) whether the Government has taken any initaitives to nominate Members of \nParliament as Directors and other posts in t he governing body of these educational \ninstitutions; \n \n(e) if so, the details thereof and if not, the reasons therefor? \n \nANSWER \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF EDUCATION \n (DR. SUBHAS SARKAR) \n \n(a) to (c)   The Central Higher Educational Institutions under the purview of Ministry of \nEducation are autonomous institutions  set up by the Acts of Parliament.  These \nInstitutions are governed by their respective Acts, Statutes, Ordinances and Regulations \nmade thereunder.  \n \nBoard of Governor s (BoGs) is the principal governing body of Centrally Funded \nTechnical Institutions (CFTIs) whereas Executive Council (EC) is the principal executive \nbody of the Central Universities.  \n \nNominations of the members in the governing body of educational institutions are made \nas per the provisions in Acts and Statutes of the institution.  Usually, these are persons \nhaving special knowledge and practical experience in the field of education, engineering \nor science.    \n \n(d) & (e) Government has not taken any initaitives to nominate Members of Parliament \nas Directors and other posts in the governing body of these educational institutions. \nNomination of members is purely governed by the provisions in respective Acts/Statutes.  \n \n***  "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|8|UNSTARRED |795", "t": "Plantations under CAMPA", "head": " \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF ENVIRONMENT, FOREST AND CLIMATE CHANGE \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 795 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 07.02.2022 \n \nPlantations under CAMPA \n \n795. SHRI KARTI P. CHIDAMBARAM: \n         \nWill the Minister of ENVIRONMENT, FOREST AND CLIMATE CHANGE be pleased \nto state: \n \n(a) whether the Government has conducted any on-ground surveys of the plantations \nmade in various States under the Compensatory Afforestation Fund Management \nand Planning Authority (CAMPA); \n(b) whether the Government has conducted any study of the accuracy of data being \nsubmitted by various States regarding plantations made under the said programme; \nand; \n(c) whether the Ministry is cognizant of media reports regarding the non-existence of \nseveral plantations under the said programme? \n \n \nANSWER \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF ENVIRONMENT, FOREST AND \nCLIMATE CHANGE  \n(SHRI ASHWINI KUMAR CHOUBEY) \n \n (a) to (b)  Plantations taken up in various States under Compensatory Afforestation Fund \nManagement and Planning Authority (CAMPA) are regularly monitored by State Forest \nDepartments through internal monitoring and evaluation mechanism of the States and \nalso through third party monitoring by external agencies. Forest Survey of India also \ncarries out analysis of geo-spatial data (polygons) of plantations being uploaded by the \nState Forest Departments on e-Green Watch portal for accuracy of location, area and \nyear of plantation. State Forest Departments also conduct on-ground surveys of the \nplantations raised under CAMPA fund and submit the Monitoring report to the \nMinistry.  \n \n(c)   As per information received from various State CAMPA Authorities, there is no \nincidences of non-existence of plantation raised under CAMPA fund reported so far.  \n \n***** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|8|UNSTARRED |796", "t": "Atmanirbhar Bharat Corner", "head": " \n \n \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF TRIBAL AFFAIRS \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO- 796 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON- 07/02/2022 \n  \nATMANIRBHAR BHARAT CORNER \n  \n796.     SHRI SANJAY KAKA PATIL: \nSHRI MAGUNTA SREENIVASULU REDDY: \nDR. BEESETTI VENKATA SATYAVATHI: \nDR. SANJEEV KUMAR SINGARI:: \n  \nWill the Minister of TRIBAL AFFAIRS be pleased to state: \n(a) the present status of setting up Atmanirbhar Bharat Corner in 100 Indian Missions/ \nEmbassies across the world; \n(b) whether the Government has devised a plan in identification of which Geographical \nIndication tagged tribal art and craft products would be promoted there; and \n(c) if so, the details thereof?? \n \n \nANSWER \n \n \n \nMINISTER OF STATE FOR TRIBAL AFFAIRS \n(SMT. RENUKA SINGH SARUTA) \n  \n(a) As per the information received from Tribal Co-Operative Marketing Development Federation \nof India (TRIFED), tribal products have been dispatched to 63 Indian Mission/Embassies \nabroad for Atmanirbhar Bharat Corners, out of which the products have already been displayed \nin 42 places as on 1.2.2022. \n(b) & (c) So far, 14 GI tagged tribal art and craft products have been sent for display in the \nAtmanirbhar Bharat Corners in the Indian Missions/Embassies abroad. \n***** \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|8|UNSTARRED |797", "t": "Illegal cutting of Trees", "head": "OIH \n \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF ENVIRONMENT, FOREST AND CLIMATE CHANGE \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 797 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON: 07.02.2022 \n \nIllegal cutting of Trees \n \n797.  SHRI RAMCHARAN BOHRA:  \n \n Will the Minister of ENVIRONMENT, FOREST AND CLIMATE CHANGE be pleased to \nstate: \n \n(a) whether it is a fact that the Government takes action only after getting complaints regarding \nillegal cutting of trees and does not take suo moto action in this regard; \n(b) if so, the details thereof and the reaction of the Government thereto; \n(c) whether people fearing mafias avoid complaining regarding illegal cutting of trees and if so, \nthe details thereof; and \n(d) the corrective measures taken by the Government in this regard and the extent to which \nthe Government is successful? \n \n \nANSWER \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF ENVIRONMENT, FOREST AND \nCLIMATE CHANGE  \n(SHRI ASHWINI KUMAR CHOUBEY) \n \n(a)  to (d) \n \nTrees in forests managed by State Forest Departments are felled as per the Working \nPlans approved by the Ministry, and their records are maintained by the State Forest \nDepartments. Protection and management of forests is primarily the responsibility \nof State Governments /Union Territory Administrations. There are strong legal \nframeworks for protection and management of tree resources which include \nNational Forest Policy 1988, Indian Forest Act, 1927, Forest (Conservation) Act, \n1980, Wildlife (Protection) Act, 1972 and State Forest Acts/State specific Tree \nPreservation Acts and Rules, etc. The State Governments /UT Administrations take \nappropriate actions in accordance with the provisions made under these Acts/ Rules \nfor regulating felling of trees.  \n***** \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|8|UNSTARRED |798", "t": "Education Loan", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF FINANCE \nDEPARTMENT OF FINANCIAL SERVICES \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. †798 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON THE 7th FEBRUARY, 2022, MAGHA 18, 1943 (SAKA) \n \nEDUCATION LOAN \n \n†798. SHRI DHARAMBIR SINGH: \nWill the Minister of FINANCE be pleased to state: \n(a) whether the Government provides education loan to students for pursuing higher \neducation; \n(b) if so, whether interest on the loan amount is charged right from the date of disbursal of the \nloan, if so, the details thereof; \n(c) whether this practice has put down extra financial burden on the students, if so, the details \nthereof;  \n(d) whether the Government is going to make provisions in the terms and conditions of \neducation loans to ensure that the interest on educational loan amount  shall only be charged \nfrom students after their education gets completed and they get employment, if so, the details \nthereof; and \n \n(e) whether the Government proposes to waive off the said education loan in case a student \nmeets with an accident and if so, the details thereof?  \n \nANSWER \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF FINANCE (DR. BHAGWAT KARAD) \n \n(a) All Scheduled Commercial Banks provide Educati on Loan to students. IBA has \nformulated and circulated to all member banks a ‘Model Education Loan Scheme’ for \nproviding financial support to meritorious students for pursuing higher education in India and \nabroad. Salient features of the scheme inter-alia include;  \n \nI. Need based finance to cover all the expenses required to complete the course viz; fee \npayable to college, hostel charges, purchase of books/ equipments/instruments/uniforms,   \netc. \n \nII. Collateral free loans upto Rs 7.5 Lakh under the Credit Guarantee Fund Scheme for \nEducation Loans (CGFSEL). \n \nIII. No Margin for loan up to Rs 7.50 Lakh. \n \nIV. Repayment period of 15 years. \n\n \nV. One year moratorium for repayment after completion of studies in all cases.  \n \nVI. Moratorium taking into account spells of unemployment/under-employment, say two or \nthree times during the life cycle of the loan. \n \nVII. Moratorium for the incubation period if the student wants to take up a start -up venture \nafter graduation. \n \n(b) & (c): Simple interest for loan is calculated from the date of disbursement of loan upto the \nend of moratorium period i.e. course period plus one year. At the start of repayment period, \nthe interest accrued is clubbed with principal & EMI is calculated accordingly. The servicing \nof interest during study period and  the moratorium period till repayment commences is \noptional for students.   \n \n(d) & (e): For the students belonging to economically weaker sections,  an i nterest subsidy \nscheme on educational loans is in place. Under the scheme full interest subsidy is avail able \nduring the period of moratorium on educational loans upto Rs 7.50 Lakh disbursed on or after \n1st April, 2009.  \nFurther, the Model Educational Loan Scheme of IBA provides for certain concessions on \neducational loans which inter-alia includes, (ii) 1% interest concession if interest is serviced \nduring the study period and subsequent moratorium period prior to the commencement of the \nrepayment, (ii) 0.5% concession in the interest rate to the girl students, (iii) rebate in Income \ntax to the extent of interest paid on education loan. \nAs per provisions of the IBA scheme, Banks may, make it mandatory to arrange for life \ninsurance policy on the students availing Education Loan.  \n******* "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|8|UNSTARRED |799", "t": "Tribal Habitation as Scheduled Areas", "head": " \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF TRIBAL AFFAIRS \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO- 799 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON- 07/02/2022 \n  \nTRIBAL HABITATION AS SCHEDULED AREAS \n  \n799.    SHRI SRIDHAR KOTAGIRI: \n           SHRI KURUVA GORANTLA MADHAV: \n           DR. SANJEEV KUMAR SINGARI: \n  \nWill the Minister of TRIBAL AFFAIRS be pleased to state: \n  \n(a) the progress of declaration 554 tribal habitations as Scheduled Area in Srikakulam, \nVizianagaram, Visakhapatnam, East and West Godavari districts, Andhra Pradesh; \n  \n(b)  the reasons for delay in the conduct of the gram sabha; and \n  \n(c)  whether the Government has taken any additional steps to expedite the process of \ndeclaration to ensure the provision of services to the region under Integrated Tribal \nDevelopment Agency? \n  \nANSWER \n  \nMINISTER OF STATE FOR TRIBAL AFFAIRS \n(SHRI BISHWESWAR TUDU) \n \n(a): That the expression ‘Scheduled Areas’ means such areas as the President may by order \ndeclare to be ‘Scheduled Areas’. Notification of a new Scheduled Area or modification to the \nextent of an existing Scheduled Area through adding, removing part or whole of a Scheduled \nArea from the list of Scheduled Area is through notification issued with the approval of the \nPresident of India as per the procedure. As per the procedure, the State Government submits a \nproposal with the recommendations of the Governor of the State to the Ministry of Tribal \nAffairs and the same is examined in the Ministry of Tribal Affairs for adherence to the \nparameters for notification of Scheduled Area. Upon examination, the process of Inter-\nMinisterial consultation (IMC) is undertaken, following the IMC process a note is submitted \nto the Cabinet for its approval. Once the Cabinet approves the proposal, the Hon’ble Minister \nof Tribal Affairs shall endorse the recommendation for obtaining the assent of the Hon’ble \nPresident of India.  After President's assent, a Constitution Order is issued through a gazette \nnotification.  \nNo proposal from the Government of Andhra Pradesh for declaration of Scheduled \nAreas in the State is pending in the Ministry..  \n  \n(b):  The Government of Andhra Pradesh has informed that the Gram Sabhas under Andhra \nPradesh PESA Rules, 2011 were notified in 2013 and statutory Gram Sabhas have been held \nregularly in addition to the Gram Sabhas being held time to time as and when required. \n(c): All the Welfare Schemes taken up by the Government of AP have been extended to \nthe regions covered by the Integrated Tribal Development Agencies (ITDAs). Regulations to protect \nthe ST communities have been implemented in V Schedule areas covered by the ITDAs, additionally. \n***** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|8|UNSTARRED |8", "t": "Stoppage at Kishanganj", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n \nLOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. 8  \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 02.02.2022 \n \nBULLET TRAIN PROJECTS \n   \n*8.          DR. SHRIKANT EKNATH SHINDE: \n      DR. SUJAY RADHAKRISHNA VIKHE PATIL:  \n  \n     Will the Minister of RAILWAYS be pleased to state: \n \n(a)  the details of the proposed new corridor projects of bullet trains; \n  \n(b)  the details of funds allocated, sanctioned and disbursed for the \nnext five years and the current year for the purpose, State/Union \nTerritory-wise; \n \n(c) whether cost of Mumbai -Ahmedabad Corridor Project has \nincreased and if so, the reasons therefor; \n \n(d) whether there is any anticipated delay in Mumbai -Ahmedabad \nCorridor and if so, the details thereof and the reasons therefor; and \n \n(e) the details of the acquisition of land between such corridors \nalong with the details of land acquired and also compensation pai d \nand rehabilitation undertaken?  \n \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF RAILWAYS, COMMUNICATIONS AND  \nELECTRONICS & INFORMATION TECHNOLOGY   \n(SHRI ASHWINI VAISHNAW) \n \n(a) to (e) : A Statement is laid on the Table of the House. \n  \n\nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PARTS (a) TO (e) OF \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. 8 BY DR. SHRIKANT EKNATH SHINDE AND \nDR. SUJAY RADHAKRISHNA VIKHE PATIL TO BE ANSWERED IN LOK \nSABHA ON 02.02.2022 REGARDING BULLET TRAIN PROJECTS  \n \n(a) and (b): Ministry of Railways has decided to prepare the Detailed \nProject Report (DPR) for the following High Speed Corridors in the \ncountry :- \n \n(i)     Delhi-Varanasi  \n(ii)    Mumbai-Nagpur \n(iii)   Delhi-Ahmedabad \n(iv)   Mumbai-Hyderabad \n(v)    Chennai-Bangaluru-Mysore \n(vi)   Varanasi-Howrah \n(vii)  Delhi-Amritsar \n \nNone of the above mentioned High Speed Corridor has been \nsanctioned; therefore, no fund has been allocated/sanctioned so far \nagainst these corridors. \n \n(c) to (e): The anticipated cost increase and time  can be fully \nascertained on ly after completion of Land Acquisition, finalization of \nall contracts and associated timelines. So far, out of 27 contract \npackages, 12 have been awarded. As on date, details of land acquired \nare as under :-   \n \n    (i)    Gujarat (98.62%) - 941.13 Ha out of  954.28 Ha  \n    (ii)   Dadra & Nagar Haveli UT (100%) - 7.90  Ha out of 7.90 Ha  \n    (iii)  Maharashtra (56.39%) – 244.63 Ha out of 433.82 Ha   \n \nThe land acquisition and Rehabilitation activities is being done in \naccordance with the “Right to Fair Compensation and Transparency in \nLand Acquisition, Rehabilitation and Resettlement (RFCTLARR) Act, \n2013”. \n***** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|8|UNSTARRED |80", "t": "Chip Exports", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF TOURISM \n \nLOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO.*80 \nANSWERED ON 07.02.2022 \n \nCREATION OF TOURISM SUB-DIVISIONS IN EMBASSIES \n \n*80.  SHRI VIJAYAKUMAR (ALIAS) VIJAY VASANTH:  \nSHRI RAVNEET SINGH BITTU:  \n \nWill the Minister of TOURISM be pleased to state: \n  \n(a)  whether the Government has any proposal to appoint tourism \nofficers and creation of tourism sub -divisions in embassies and \nmissions abroad to promote Indian tourist destinations abroad;  \n(b)  if so, the details thereof and the extent  to which tourism in the \ncountry is likely to be promoted as a result of this proposal;  \n(c)  the time by which the above proposal is likely to be \nimplemented;  \n(d)  the details of any study or assessment done to assess the \npotential impact of this proposa l on the domestic tourism \nindustry; and  \n(e)  whether the Government is taking any other measures to \npromote the domestic tourist destinations in various other \ncountries of the world, if so, the details thereof and if not, the \nreasons therefor? \n \nANSWER \nMINISTER OF TOURISM                (SHRI G. KISHAN REDDY) \n \n(a) to (e): A Statement is laid on the table of the House. \n******* \n \n \n \n\n \nSTATEMENT IN REPLY TO PARTS (a) TO (e) OF LOK SABHA STARRED \nQUESTION NO.*80 ANSWERED ON 07.02.2022 REGARDING CREATION \nOF TOURISM SUB-DIVISIONS IN EMBASSIES. \n \n(a) to (c):  Ministry of External Affairs has designated Tourism \nOfficers in the Indian Missions of top 20 s ource markets in October, \n2021 which is attached at Annexure.  \n \n(d) to (e):  The Ministry of Tourism, through its 8 India Tourism Offices \nOverseas endeavors to position India as a preferred tourism \ndestination in the tourism generating markets to promote various \ntourism products and destinations and to increase India’s share in the \nglobal tourism market. The objectives are  met through an integrated \nmarketing and promotional strategy, global media campaign and a \nsynergized promotional measures in association with the Travel trade, \nState Governments and Indian Missions overseas. \n \n***** \n\nANNEXURE \nSTATEMENT IN REPLY TO PARTS (a ) to (c ) OF LOK SABHA STARRED \nQUESTION NO.*80 ANSWERED ON 07.02.2022 REGARDING CREATION \nOF TOURISM SUB-DIVISIONS IN EMBASSIES. \nSl. No. Country \n1.  Australia \n2.  Canada \n3.  China \n4.  France \n5.  Germany \n6.  Italy \n7.  Japan \n8.  Malaysia \n9.  Myanmar \n10.  Oman \n11.  Portugal \n12.  Russia \n13.  Singapore \n14.  South Korea \n15.  Spain \n16.  Sri Lanka \n17.  Thailand \n18.  The Netherlands \n19.  UK \n20.  USA \n \n****** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|8|UNSTARRED |800", "t": "Vacant Posts in IIT/NIT", "head": " \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF EDUCATION \nDEPARTMENT OF HIGHER EDUCATION \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 800 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 07.02.2022 \n \nVacant Posts in IIT/NIT \n \n†800. SHRI VIJAY BAGHEL: \n  SHRI SUNIL KUMAR SONI: \n \nWill the Minister of Education be pleased to state: \n \n(a) the number of posts of Chairme n and others vacan cies in the governing \n body of Indian Institute of Technology (IIT) and National Institute of \n Technology (NIT) in the country; \n \n(b) whether the Government has set any timeframe to fill these vacant  posts; \n and  \n \n(c) if so, the details thereof and if not, the reasons therefor?  \n \n \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF EDUCATION \n \n(DR. SUBHAS SARKAR) \n \n \n(a): At present, 08 positions of Chairmen in IITs and 22 positions of \nChairmen in NITs are vacant. Further, 03 posts of Directors in IITs and 10 \nposts of Directors in NITs are vacant.  Out of these  order/offer of appointment \nhave been issued with respect to 01 IIT and 10 NITs. \n(b) & (c): The nomination/selection of Chairm en and other posts is a \ncontinuous process.  \n***** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|8|UNSTARRED |801", "t": "Development of Omkareshwar Temple", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF TOURISM \n \nLOK SABHA \n   UNSTARRED QUESTION NO.+801 \nANSWERED ON 07.02.2022 \n \nDEVELOPMENT OF OMKARESHWAR TEMPLE \n \n†801. SHRI GYANESHWAR PATIL:  \n \nWill the Minister of TOURISM be pleased to state:  \n \n(a)  whether the Government has e laborate plans to develop the \nOmkareshwar temple complex in line with other Jyotirlingas from \nthe tourism point of view along with the steps taken by the \nGovernment in this regard;  \n(b)  whether the Government has made any plans for the \nredevelopment and maintenance of the Narmada Ghats adjoining \nthe Omkareshwar temple complex for the benefit of pilgrims; and  \n(c)  if so, the details thereof and if not, the future plans of the \nGovernment in this regard? \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF TOURISM    (SHRI G. KISHAN REDDY) \n \n(a) to (c):  Yes, Sir.  On the basis of the proposal received from the \nState Government of Madhya Pradesh the project “Development of \nOmkareshwar under PRASHAD Scheme” has been approved by the \nMinistry of Tourism in the year 2017 -18.  Approved cost of th e project \nis Rs. 44.83 crore. The project includes the works for development of \nGau Ghat at the Narmada River. \n \nThe execution of the project has been completed by the State \nGovernment in all respect. \n****** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|8|UNSTARRED |802", "t": "Sickle Cell Disease among Tribal Population", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF TRIBAL AFFAIRS \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO- 802 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON- 07/02/2022 \n  \nSICKLE CELL DISEASE AMONG TRIBAL POPULATION \n  \n802.     SHRIMATI RITA BAHUGUNA JOSHI: \n            SHRI SHYAM SINGH YADAV: \n  \nWill the Minister of TRIBAL AFFAIRS be pleased to state: \n(a) whether the Government has conducted nationwide screening for Sickle Cell Disease (SCD) among the tribal \npopulation of the country; \n(b) if so, the details thereof; \n(c) the steps taken by the Government for the preventive measure and its treatment in the tribal \npopulation; \n(d) whether the Government will promote more affected tribal persons to get voluntarily registered on SCD \nsupport centre to get information about the disease and resources to get help and if so, the details thereof? \n(e) the number of tribal women suffering from sickle cell anaemia in Uttar Pradesh; and \n(f) the steps which the Government is taking to eliminate sickle cell anaemia amongst tribal women? \nANSWER \nMINISTER OF STATE FOR TRIBAL AFFAIRS \n(SMT. RENUKA SINGH SARUTA) \n  \n(a) & (b) Ministry of Tribal affairs has conducted screening of tribal population in collaboration with ICMR and \nDepartment of Biotechnology. Out of the 1,13,83,664 persons screened in different States, about 8.75% \n(9,96,368) tested positive (Trait –949057, Disease – 47311). \n(c) to (f): Public Health is a state subject and Ministry of Health and Family welfare is the sectoral Ministry for \nall health issues, including sickle cell.  National Health Mission has prepared a comprehensive guideline to control \nand prevent Haemoglobinopathies, including Sickle Cell Disease, and has disseminated the same to the States. \nThis includes pre-natal diagnosis,counseling and setting up of early intervention centers to prevent and treat the \ncomplications arising from the disease. At present there is no permanent cure for the disease. However, with good \nmanagement of disease, severity and complications can be curtailed to improve the quality of life and life span of \nthe people suffering with the disease. In consultation with Department of Health Research, Ministry of Tribal \nAffairs has circulated advisories on Sickle Cell Disease with a protocol for premarital counseling of people with \n\nsickle cell trait (carrier). A total of about Rs. 60.00 Crore has been released to the States seeking grants to tackle \nthe Sickle Cell Anemia, including screening.  State wise details for fund released is at Annexure 1. \nFurther, details of various projects undertaken by the Ministry of Tribal Affairs are as under: \n(i)  Sickle Cell Disease Support Corner (https://scdcorner.in/) has been developed to create awareness about SCD \nand to connect these individuals to welfare schemes, disease-specific healthcare services and validated health \ninformation and to enable data-driven policy insights and strategic inputs. In collaboration with organisation like \nPirmal Swasthya, USAID and Novartis,Ministry has started \"Unmukt\" program on pilot basis in 2 districts one \nin Chattisgarh and  the other In Jharkhandd to create awarenes about the disease. \n(ii)  This Ministry in consultation with Ministry of Health and Family Welfare is developing a treatise on SCD \nfor training of trainers in medical colleges and modules for training of medical officers at District hospitals and \nintegrated centers.  \n(iii)   The Ministry has sanctioned a research project which aims to explore naturopathy and yogic methods for \ncuring sickle cell anaemia disease. \n(iv)  The Ministry has sanctioned a project to Tribal Research Institute (TRI) Odisha of Mapping of Sickle Cell \nAnaemia in the Tribal Sub Plan Area  among the Tribal Communities of the State and a Compendium of Empirical \nStudies & Its findings on Sickle Cell Anaemia among the Tribal Communities of ODISHA. \n(v)  A project ‘Diagnosis, IEC and Nutri support for sickle cell anaemia and Thalassemia affected patients’ has \nbeen sanctioned to TRI Telangana. \n(vi)  A project entitled ‘Mapping of Sickle Cell Anemia  among the Tribal Communities, Collation and \ncompilation of data, mapping of organizations working in Sickle Cell, Data base of master trainers on sickle cell \nin co-ordination with MoHFW,  Data sharing mechanism and mapping of Blood Banks availability ’ has been \ngiven to National Tribal Research Institute (NTRI). \n(vii). States have been asked to seek funds under Grants under article 275(1) for infrastructural requirements \nrelated to diagnostic facilities and testing.   \nDedicated Health Cell has been established in Ministry to focus upon health issues holistically including Sickle \nCell Anemia among ST population including tribal women.    \nDepartment of Empowerment of person with Disabilities has issued  notification for considering SCD as disability \nand issuing  disability certificate more than 80% disability valid for 3 years.  \nState-wise details of screening of Sickle Cell Disease in tribals is at Annexure 2. Gender specific informati"}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|8|UNSTARRED |803", "t": "Centrally Sponsored Schemes for Employment", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF LABOUR AND EMPLOYMENT \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 803 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 07TH FEBRUARY, 2022 \n \nCENTRALLY SPONSORED SCHEMES FOR EMPLOYMENT  \n \n803.  SHRI JANARDAN SINGH SIGRIWAL: \n \n Will the Minister of LABOUR AND EMPLOYMENT be pleased to state: \n \n(a) the details of Centrally Sponsored Schemes for the purpose to provide \nsufficient employment opportunities in the rural areas and small towns \nin the country; \n \n(b) whether the Government proposes any special schemes to provide job \nopportunities in the said areas to check migration of people to \nmetropolitan cities; and \n \n(c) if so, the details thereof along with the funds earmarked for the \npurpose? \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF STATE FOR LABOUR AND EMPLOYMENT \n(SHRI RAMESWAR TELI) \n \n(a) to (c): Employment generation coupled with improving employability \nin the country including rural areas and small towns is the priority of the \nGovernment. Multi-pronged strategies are being taken by the Government \nto address issues relating to employment opportunity through Centrally \nSponsored Schemes viz. Mahatma Gandhi National Rural Employment \nGuarantee Scheme (MGNREGS), Deen dayal Antyoday Yojana - National \nRural Livelihood Mission (DAY -NRLM), Deendayal Upadhyay - Gramin \nKaushalya Yojana (DDU -GKY), Pradhan Mantri Gram Sadak Yojana \n(PMGSY), Shyama Prasad Mukherjee RURban Mission, National Career \nService (NCS) etc. \n\n         Further, the Government of India has  taken various steps for \ngenerating employment in the country. The Government of India has \nannounced Aatmanirbhar Bharat package to provide stimulus to business \nand to mitigate the adverse impact of Covid 19. Under this package, the \nGovernment is providing  fiscal stimulus of more than Rs. Twenty Seven \nlakh crore. This package comprises of various long term schemes/ \nprogrammes/ policies for making the country self -reliant and to create \nemployment opportunities. \n \nThe Government launched the Garib Kalyan Rojgar Abhiyaan (GKRA) \nof 125 days on 20th June, 2020 to boost employment and livelihood \nopportunities for returnee migrant workers and similarly affected persons \nincluding youth in rural areas, in 116 selected districts across 6 States of \nBihar, Jharkhand, Madhya Pradesh, Odisha, Rajasthan and Uttar Pradesh. \nThe Abhiyaan has achieved an employment generation of 50.78 crore \npersondays with a total expenditure of Rs 39,293 crore. \n \n  Aatmanirbhar Bharat RojgarYojana (ABRY) has been launched with \neffect from 1st October, 2020 as part of Atmanirbhar Bharat package 3.0 \nto incentivize employers for creation of new employment along with \nsocial security benefits and restoration of loss of employment during \nCovid-19 pandemic. This scheme being implemented through the \nEmployees’ Provident Fund Organisation (EPFO), seeks to reduce the \nfinancial burden of the employers and encourages them to hire more \nworkers. The terminal date for registration of beneficiaries has been \nextended from 30.06.2021 to 31.03.2022. Benefits of Rs.3 435/- crore have \nbeen provided to 46.89 lakh beneficiaries through 1.26 lakh \nestablishments till 29.01.2022.  \n \n            Prime Minister Street Vendor’s AtmaNirbhar Nidhi (PM SVANidhi) \nScheme has been launched on June 01, 2020 to provide working capital \nloans to Street Vendors, vending in urban areas, to resume their \nbusinesses, which were impacted adversely due to COVID -19. Under this \nscheme, credit worth Rs.  3,054 crore to 30.2 lakh street vendors as on \n30.11.2021 \n  \n\nPradhan Mantri Mudra Yojana  (PMMY) is being implemented by the \nGovernment for facilitating self-employment. Under PMMY, collateral free \nloans upto Rs. 10 lakh, are extended to micro/small business enterprises \nand to individuals to enable them to setup or expand their business \nactivities. Upto 21.01.2022, Rs.32.12 crore loans were sanctioned under \nthe scheme. The Production Linked Incentive Schemes being \nimplemented by the Government have potential for creating 60 lakh new \njobs. \n \n           PM Gati Shakti is a transformative approach for economic growth \nand sustainable development. The approach is driven by seven engines, \nnamely, Roads, Railways, Airports, Ports, Mass Transport, Waterways and \nLogistics Infrastructure. This approach is powered by Clean Energy and \nSabka Prayas leading to  huge job and entrepreneurial opportunities for \nall. \n  \n         The Government of India is encouraging various projects involving \nsubstantial investment and public expenditure on schemes like Prime \nMinister’s Employment Generation Programme (PMEGP)of the M inistry of \nMicro, Small & Medium Enterprises, Deen Dayal Antodaya Yojana -National \nUrban Livelihoods Mission (DAY -NULM) of  the Ministry of Housing & \nUrban Affairs etc. for employment generation. \n \n           Besides these initiatives, various flagship progr ammes of the \nGovernment such as Make in India, Digital India, Smart City Mission, Atal \nMission for Rejuvenation and Urban Transformation, H"}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|8|UNSTARRED |804", "t": "Climate Change Mitigation Actions", "head": " \n \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF ENVIRONMENT, FOREST AND CLIMATE CHANGE \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION No. 804 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 07.02.2022 \n \n Climate Change Mitigation Actions \n \n804. SHRI SAPTAGIRI SANKAR ULAKA: \n \nWill the Minister of ENVIRONMENT, FOREST AND CLIMATE CHANGE be pleased to \nstate: \n \n(a)  whether the Government is aware that climate change mitigation actions such as \nplantations are coming up on customary lands and forests of adivasis and forest dwellers \nand undermining their rights under the Forest Rights Act (FRA) and the Panchayat \n(Extension to Scheduled Areas) Act (PESA); and  \n(b)  the mechanisms the Government has in place to ensure that actions taken to combat \nclimate change are compliant with the FRA and PESA? \n \nANSWER \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF ENVIRONMENT, FOREST AND \nCLIMATE CHANGE  \n(SHRI ASHWINI KUMAR CHOUBEY) \n \n(a) and (b) Plantations in forest areas are undertaken by State/Union Territory (UT) \nForest Departments as per approved Working Plans, excluding the areas \nwhere individual forest rights titles are issued under the Forest Rights Act, \n2006. Wherever Community Forest Rights (CFR) have been recognized, \nplantations and other activities are taken up in consultation with local \ncommunities as per the approved Working Plans and Micro Plans prepared \nby CFR management committee constituted under rule 4 (e) of the \nScheduled Tribes and Other Traditional Forest Dwellers (Recognition of \nForest Rights) Rules, 2007.  \n \nThere are no reports from States/UTsto show that the rights of adivasis and \nforest dwellers vested under FRA, 2006 and PESA, 1996 are being \nundermined due to Climate Change mitigation action such as plantations. \n \n*** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|8|UNSTARRED |805", "t": "Private Schools and Universities", "head": " \n \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF EDUCATION \nDEPARTMENT OF HIGHER EDUCATION \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 805 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 07.02.2022 \n \nPrivate Schools and Universities \n \n805. SHRI PASHUPATI NATH SINGH: \n  \nWill the Minister of EDUCATION be pleased to state: \n \n(a) whether it is a fact that the criteria for Government and private schools and colleges are same \nbut students prefer to attend Government colleges instead of private colleges and private schools in \ncomparison to Government schools;  \n \n(b) if so, the reasons therefor;  \n \n(c) whether the New Education Policy, 2020 is likely to bring any change in the above mentioned \ntrend; and  \n \n(d) if so, the proposal of the Government in this regard? \n \nANSWER \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF EDUCATION  \n(DR. SUBHAS SARKAR) \n \n(a) to (d): As per National Education Policy 2020 (NEP 2020), the approach to equity and \ninclusion must be common across school and higher education. NEP 2020 inter-alia provides that \npublic and private schools are to be assessed and accredited on the same criteria, benchmarks, and \nprocesses, emphasizing online and offline public disclosure and transparency. NEP 2020 also \nproposes similar standards of audit and disclosure as a 'not-for-profit' entity to all the education \ninstitutions. Surpluses, if any, will be reinvested in the educational sector. Similarly, in higher \neducation, all HEIs - public and private - shall be treated on par observing common guidelines. \n \n \n******* "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|8|UNSTARRED |806", "t": "Higher Education Commission of India", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF EDUCATION \nDEPARTMENT OF HIGHER EDUCATION \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION No. 806 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 07.02.2022 \nHigher Education Commission of India \n806. SHRI SUSHIL KUMAR SINGH: \nWill the Minister of EDUCATION be pleased to state: \n(a) whether there is a proposal for setting up Higher Education Commission of India (HECI); \n(b) if so, the details thereof and the status and concrete timelines of setting up of HECI; \n(c) whether HECI will replace autonomous bodies  like the Universi ty Grants Commission \n(UGC), All India  Council for Technical Education (AICTE) and National  Council for Teacher \nEducation (NCTE);  \n(d) if so, the details thereof;  \n(e) whether the Government is planning to disband  UGC, AICTE and NCTE and if so, whether \nit won’t lead to centralisation of powers in one body; and  \n(f) if so, the detail thereof? \nANSWER \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF EDUCATION \n(DR. SUBHAS SARKAR) \n(a) to (f): The Ministry of Education has announced the National Education Policy (NEP) 2020 \non 29.07.2020 after obtaining approval of the Union Cabinet. The NEP-2020 envisions setting \nup of a Higher Education Commission of India as an umbrella body with four independent \nverticals to perform distinct functions of regulation, accreditation, funding, and academic \nstandard setting. Accordingly, the Ministry is in the process of drafting a Bill for establishment \nof the Higher Education Commission of India.  \n***** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|8|UNSTARRED |807", "t": "ESI Dispensaries", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF LABOUR AND EMPLOYMENT \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 807 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 07.02.2022 \n \nESI DISPENSARIES \n \n807. SHRI LAVU SRI KRISHNA DEVARAYALU: \n  \nWill the Minister of LABOUR AND EMPLOYMENT be pleased to \nstate: \n \n(a)the details of the number of ESI dispensaries in Narasaraopet, \nAndhra Pradesh and their operational status; \n(b)whether it is true that the Ministry has decided to construct a new \nESI hospital in Guntur district of Andhra Pradesh with 100 -bed \ncapacity; \n(c)if so, the details thereof; and \n(d)whether the Ministry is going to allot work to CPWD, if so, the time \nby which the hospital is expected to become operational? \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF STATE FOR LABOUR AND EMPLOYMENT \n(SHRI RAMESWAR TELI) \n \n(a):  Primary, secondary and super specialty medical facilities to \nEmployees’ State Insurance (ESI) beneficiaries of Narasaraopet are \nprovided through ESI Scheme (ESIS) dispensary, Ganapavaram, ESIS \nhospital, Vijayawada and 7 tie-up hospitals.   \n(b) to (d): It had been decided to set up a 100 -bedded ESIC hospital in \nGuntur district of Andhra Pradesh and the project is at present  in land \nidentification/allotment stage.  Construction agency is decided after \npossession of the land and approval of estimates. \n \n****** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|8|UNSTARRED |808", "t": "Training under PMKVY", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF SKILL DEVELOPMENT AND ENTREPRENEURSHIP \n \nLOK SABHA \n \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 808 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 07.02.2022 \n  \nTRAINING UNDER PMKVY \n \n808. DR. PRITAM GOPINATHRAO MUNDE:  \nSHRI RAHUL RAMESH SHEWALE: \nSHRI CHANDRA SEKHAR SAHU: \n \nWill the Minister of SKILL DEVELOPMENT AND ENTREPRE NEURSHIP be pleased \nto state: \n \n(a) whether it is a fact that no training centres h ave been established under Pradhan \nMantri Kaushal Vikas Yojana (PMKVY) so far; \n \n(b)  if so, the reasons therefor; \n \n(c)  whether it is a fact that short term training is being implemented through empanelled \ntraining centres; \n \n(d) if so, the details thereof; \n \n(e) whether the empanelled training centres are pas sing the times in the name of training \nwhich is a fraud for the beneficiaries/ trainees; \n \n(f) if so, whether the Union Government has receive d complaints regarding fraud \ncommitted by the empanelled training centres; \n \n(g) if so, the details thereof, State-wise; and \n \n(h) the action taken by the Union Government in thi s regard? \n \nANSWER \n  \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE \nMINISTRY OF SKILL DEVELOPMENT AND ENTREPRENEURSHIP \n(SHRI RAJEEV CHANDRASEKHAR) \n  \n(a) and (b) Under Skill India Mission, Ministry of Skill Development and Entrepreneurship is \nimplementing a flagship scheme Pradhan Mantri Kaush al Vikas Yojana (PMKVY). Under \nPMKVY, short term training is being imparted in acc redited and affiliated skill development \ntraining centres across the country. \n \nUnder PMKVY, since inception, i.e., 2015 till 31.12 .2021, short term training has been \nimparted in 30,100 skill development training centr es (TCs) including PMKKs across the \ncountry. These TCs were established without funding support from the Ministry.  \n\n  \n         Further, Ministry of Skill Development and  Entrepreneurship (MSDE) promotes \nestablishment of model training centres in every di strict of the country known as Pradhan \nMantri Kaushal Kendra (PMKK).   As on 15.01.2022, 813 PMKKs have been allocated ac ross \nthe country; out of which, 719 have been establishe d. Further, for the establishment of \nPMKKs, Ministry through National Skill Development Corporation (NSDC) provides capital \nexpenditure upto 75% of the project investment as w ell as operational support to industrial \npartner / corporate for setting up of PMKK. PMKK ce ntres are provided loan from NSDC up to \nRs. 70 lakh to the PPP partner. \n \n(c) and (d)        Above reply (a) may be referred to.  \n \n(e)       No, Sir. Under PMKVY, short term training is being imparted through skill development \ntraining centres (TCs) selected through robust accr editation and affiliation process on Skill \nIndia Portal (SIP). TCs are being monitored effecti vely through various methodologies \nincluding information technology (IT) interventions  and measures namely; self-audit reporting, \ncall validations, surprise visits and monitoring th rough the Skill India Portal (SIP), Aadhaar \nEnabled Biometric Attendance System (AEBAS), social media platform, etc.  \n  \nFurther, in order to improve the monitoring under P MKVY, District Skill Committee \n(DSC) is being involved and entrusted with the moni toring under PMKVY 3.0. DSC acts as an \non-ground monitoring agency for conducting inspection of TCs.  \n  \n(f) to (h)          Under the scheme, PMKVY Monitor ing Committee review the cases related to \nmonitoring issues of the stakeholders. Under the scheme, there is provision for taking suitable \naction against erring / non-compliant training cent res / stakeholders as per penalty grid \nframework. Based on the penalty grid, National Skil l Development Corporation (NSDC), the \nimplementing agency of PMKVY under MSDE, has suspen ded training centres for non-\ncompliance of PMKVY guidelines on multiple parameters and periodically publishes the list on \nPMKVY official website. \n  \nUnder PMKVY, some complaints were received on vario us parameters in the Ministry, \nand NSDC and appropriate action on every complaint was taken. So far, 17 FIRs were lodged \nagainst the complaint received by the Ministry. Als o, based on the monitoring framework of \nPMKVY, 307 Training Centres (TCs) have been suspend ed across the different locations. \nThe State-wise no. of TCs suspended is given at Annexure.  \n \n \n \n  \n\nAnnexure \n \nState-wise no. of suspended TCs under PMKVY: \n \nS. No.  State  No. of TCs  \n1.  Arunachal Pradesh 2 \n2.  Assam 5 \n3.  Bihar 5 \n4.  Chandigarh 3 \n5.  Chhattisgarh 6 \n6.  Delhi 10 \n7.  Gujarat 6 \n8.  Haryana 20 \n9.  Himachal Pradesh 6 \n10.  Jammu and Kashmir 14 \n11.  Jharkhand 9 \n12.  Karnataka 4 \n13.  Kerala 5 \n14.  Madhya Pradesh 11 \n15.  Maharashtra 11 \n16.  Nagaland 2 \n17.  Odisha 12 \n18.  Puducherry 2 \n19.  Punjab 6 \n20.  Rajasthan 67 \n21.  Tamil Nadu 15 \n22.  Telangana 4 \n23.  Tripura 4 \n24.  Uttar Pradesh 67 \n25.  Uttarakhand 2 \n26.  West Bengal 9 \nTotal  307  \n \n****** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|8|UNSTARRED |809", "t": "Voluntary Organisations working for Welfare of Scheduled Tribes", "head": "  \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF TRIBAL AFFAIRS \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION No- 809  \nTO BE ANSWERED ON- 07/02/2022 \n  \nVOLUNTARY ORGANISATIONS WORKING FOR WELFARE OF SCHEDULED TRIBES \n  \n809.  SHRI L.S. TEJASVI SURYA \nWill the Minister of TRIBAL AFFAIRS be pleased to state: - \n(a) the total grant-in-aid released by the Government to voluntary organisations working for the welfare of \nScheduled Tribes in Karnataka in the years 2019-2021; \n  \n(b) the details of the projects being financed by the grants-in-aid in Scheduled and Non-Scheduled areas; \n  \n(c) category-wise breakup of the projects being provided grants-in-aid; and \n  \n(d) the process of application, scrutiny and review of the afore mentioned aids being granted to the voluntary \norganizations? \n  \nANSWER \n  \nMINISTER OF STATE FOR TRIBAL AFFAIRS \n(SMT. RENUKA SINGH SARUTA) \n  \n(a) to (c): Grant-in-aid released by the Government to voluntary organizations working for the welfare of \nScheduled Tribes in Karnataka in the years 2019-2021 is placed at Annexure. \n  \n(d):  Any Non-Governmental Organization (NGO) seeking funds under the scheme of \"Grants in Aid to \nVoluntary Organizations working for the welfare of STs\" is required to submit its application on dedicated \nonline NGO portal https://ngo.tribal.gov.in as and when portal is opened for receiving applications and \nfollowing procedure is followed before the grants are released.   \n The NGO is required to register itself on NITI Aayog's Darpan Portal and obtain an Unique ID. Using \nthis Unique ID, the organization has to register on Ministry of Tribal Affairs' NGO Portal \nhttps://ngo.tribal.gov.in. \n The application is required to be recommended by the concerned district and state authorities after \nnecessary inspection of the project  \n \n At Ministry level, the new projects recommended by State are screened and placed  before the Project \nApproval Committee headed by the Secretary, Ministry of Tribal Affairs, along with the \nrecommendations of the inspecting agency and finally approved by the Minister for Tribal Affairs. \n The funds to the organization are released with financial concurrence of the competent authorities online \nthrough Public Financial Management System (PFMS) directly into the bank accounts of the NGO. \n \n The NGO is required to update the expenditure incurred by on Expenditure-Advance-Transfer (EAT) \nModule of PFMS.  \n To ensure transparency in the processing of the applications, the NGO can also see the progress of its \napplication on the portal in real time basis. Officials from the Ministry are also deputed to visit the \nproject sites and submit their reports on the functioning of the projects. \n \n  \n\nANNEXURE \n \nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PART (a) TO (c) OF LOK SABHA UNSTARRED \nQUESTION NO. 809 FOR ANSWER ON 07.02.2022 REGARDING “VOLUNTARY \nORGANISATIONS WORKING FOR WELFARE OF SCHEDULED TRIBES”. \n  \nDETAILS OF FUNDS RELEASED TO NON-GOVERNMENTAL ORGANIZATIONS IN THE STATE OF \nKARNATAKA FROM 2019-20 TO 2020-21  \n  \nUNDER THE SCHEME OF GRANT-IN-AID TO VOLUNTARY ORGANIZATIONS WORKING FOR \nWELFARE OF STs. \nName_of_NGO Scheduled \nArea / Non-\nScheduled \nArea \n2019-20 2020-21 (As on 31.1.2022)  \nEDUCATION \nSECTOR \nHEALTH \nSECTOR \nEDUCATION \nSECTOR \nHEALTH \nSECTOR \nAMBEDKAR EDUCATION \nSOCIETY \nNon-\nScheduled \nArea \n₹ 4,92,739 - - - \nASHIRWAD RURAL \nDEVELOPMENT TRUST \nNon-\nScheduled \nArea \n- ₹ 23,39,600  - ₹ 26,12,722  \nBHARATHI EDUCATION TRUST Non-\nScheduled \nArea \n₹ 21,87,690 - ₹ 4,96,207 - \nHARIHARAGRAMINABHIVRUDHI \nSANGHA \nNon-\nScheduled \nArea \n- ₹ 7,78,800  - ₹ 12,26,457  \nNAVAJYOTI INSTITUTE FOR \nSELF HELP AND RURAL \nDEVELOPMENT \nNon-\nScheduled \nArea \n- - ₹ 2,57,367 - \nPRAGATHI RURAL \nDEVELOPMENT SOCIETY \nScheduled \nArea \n₹ 21,60,360 - ₹ 9,78,368 - \nSAMARPANA DEVELOPMENT \nORGANIZATION  \nNon-\nScheduled \nArea \n₹ 8,86,833 - - - \nSANT KABIRDAS EDUCATION \nSOCIETY \nNon-\nScheduled \nArea \n₹ 21,95,246 - - - \nSRI MANJUNATHASWAMY \nVIDYA SAMSTHE \nNon-\nScheduled \nArea \n₹ 17,97,368 - - - \nSRI SWAMY SARVA DHARMA \nSHARANALAYA TRUST \nNon-\nScheduled \nArea \n₹ 12,99,298 ₹ 22,71,150 - - \nSWAMI VIVEKANANDA YOUTH \nMOVEMENT \nNon-\nScheduled \nArea \n₹ 49,97,837 ₹ 32,95,212 ₹ 20,26,266 ₹ 40,53,657 \nVIVEKANANDA  GIRIJANA \nKALYANA KENDRA \nNon-\nScheduled \nArea \n- ₹ 7,95,336  - - \n  ₹ 1,60,17,371 ₹ 94,80,098 ₹ 37,58,208 ₹ 78,92,836 \n***** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|8|UNSTARRED |81", "t": "Shifting from Coal Based Economy", "head": "�\n������������������� �\n����������������� �\n��� ������ �\n�� �������������������� �� �\n���������������������������� �\n��\n�������������������������������� �\n�\n�� ������������������ ��\n�\n�����������������������������������������������\n�\n������������ ��� ������������ ����������� ���� ���� ��������� ����������� ��������\n�������������� �������������������\n�������������������������������������� ���������������������������������������\n���������� ���������������������������������\n������������������������������������������������� �������������������������� ���\n���������������������������������������������� �\n�����������������������������������������������������������\n�\n������ �\n��\n����������� ������������������������������������